From 042dcebd1a07379e29857985ddb3adc155ed6b18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:58:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/53] B70-V2-MOE: accept the v7 wheel (W4A8 apply with the
 fused gemm1 epilogue branch)

v7 wheel: XpuFusedMoe._apply_kernel unchanged (32c13063d42ad5ae);
b70_moe_w4a8.apply gained the B70_W4A8_FUSED_ACT load_glu_op branch (2bdb73e8f7e4f4b8). The
cutlass replica now carries that branch (absent on v6, so v6 behaviour is unchanged) and both
fingerprints are accepted. Tests run the replica against the v6 and v7 bodies, fused on/off.
---
 tests/kernels/test_b70_v2_kcut.py             | 56 +++++++++++----
 .../layers/fused_moe/b70_moe_kcut.py          | 72 +++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

